                        <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_814">Bredgar, Kent.
                                Parish church</orgName>
                            <p>Fol. 3v: <q>To haue in mynd that <persName key="person_3952"
                                        role="dnr">sir Iohn' mone</persName> sumtyme wycary of
                                    bradgare gawe this goode bybill' the wyche is the grounde of
                                    holy wrytte of bothe the new lawe and the olde to the chyrch of
                                    bradgare to goddes worshyppe and that his bredyrn of this
                                    forsayd chyrche of bradgare schuld rede upon hit whane hit plese
                                    hem. And thei to hawe syr Iohn mone in mynde and prei for his
                                    soule And also maystir vycary of bradgare that is to say euery
                                    vycary in his tyme is putte in truste that this bouk and the
                                    other boukes that be chened schuld be welle gouerned as thei
                                    owth to be. And the forsade syr Iohn mone decessed fro the
                                    tribulacion of this world to god the viij day of Iunii the yere
                                    of oure lord Ih<ex>es</ex>u crist a thousand foure hundreth thre
                                    score and xiiij vpon the wyche soule owre lord hawe
                                    m<ex>er</ex>cy amen.</q></p></provenance>
                        <provenance type="MLGB3_LaterOwners"><q><persName>Robert Elwick</persName>
                                vic' de bredgar anno 1700</q> (fol. 1)</provenance>
